<title>USA: San Antonio feeder cattle prices steady-up $2 - USDA.</title>
<headline>San Antonio feeder cattle prices steady-up $2 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers and heifers were steady to firm, except 400-500 lb steers and 500-600 lb heifers steady to $2.00 higher, compared to last week, USDA said. Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 300-600 lb feeder steers and heifers.</p>
<p>Supply included around 10 percent slaughter cows and bulls; 30 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs with balance mostly feeder cattle under 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>70.00-80.25, pkg 84.00; 700-800 lbs 66.00-70.25; few 800-825</p>
<p>lbs 66.50-69.50. Medium and Large 1-2 - 300-400 lbs</p>
<p>79.00-86.00; 400-500 lbs 73.00-79.00; 500-600 lbs 66.00-74.00;</p>
<p>few 700-1000 lbs 55.00-64.50.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>66.00-70.50, pkg 73.50; few 700-750 lbs 66.25-68.25. Medium</p>
<p>and Large 1-2 - 500-700 lbs 58.00-67.50.</p>
<p>Receipts - 621    Last Week - 1,109   Last Year - 931</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
